---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import profile from '../data/profile.json';
---
<Base title="Ilian Aigner — B2B Sales, Customer Discovery & STRK" description="STRK co-founder. Top 20 Lerner Sales Competition semi-finalist. University of Delaware student seeking U.S. B2B sales, SDR, and BDR internships." kind="home">
<section class="home-hero story-hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
 <div class="hero-copy">
  <p class="hero-kicker">Seeking U.S. B2B sales / SDR / BDR internships</p>
  <h1 id="hero-title">Ilian<br /><span>Aigner.</span></h1>
  <p class="hero-statement">Ambition is easy to claim.<br />I’d rather show the work.</p>
  <p class="hero-intro">I’m a STRK co-founder and University of Delaware entrepreneurship student. I’ve coached teams, supported lead qualification, and reached the Top 20 in a 122-person sales competition.</p>
  <div class="action-row"><a class="button button-primary" href="/work/">View my work ↗</a><a class="button button-outline" href="/ilian-aigner-cv.pdf" download>Download CV ↓</a></div>
 </div>
 <figure class="hero-photo"><img src="/assets/images/ilian-portrait-shirt-1200.jpg" srcset="/assets/images/ilian-portrait-shirt-700.jpg 700w, /assets/images/ilian-portrait-shirt-1200.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 55vw" width="1200" height="1200" alt="Ilian Aigner in a navy suit with a neatly closed white shirt" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption>Entrepreneurship student. STRK co-founder.</figcaption></figure>
 <div class="hero-bottom"><span>University of Delaware · Expected Fall 2028</span><a href="#approach">Follow the story ↓</a></div>
</section>
<section class="story-opening shell" id="story"><p class="section-label">The ambition has a starting point.</p><h2>Before the pitch,<br />there’s a person.</h2><p>I’ve coached young athletes, worked with prospective clients, and helped turn customer conversations into a startup direction. Different settings. The same challenge: understand who’s in front of you, communicate clearly, and earn the next step.</p></section>
<div class="story-journey shell" id="approach">
 <aside class="journey-spine" aria-label="My story"><span class="journey-endpoint">Where I started</span><div class="journey-track" aria-hidden="true"><span class="journey-fill"></span><span class="journey-marker"></span></div><strong class="journey-current">Coaching in Hamburg</strong><span class="journey-endpoint">What I’m building</span></aside>
 <div class="journey-chapters">
  <section class="story-chapter" id="about" data-journey-label="Coaching in Hamburg"><p class="chapter-place">Hamburg · 2022–2025</p><h2>First, learn<br />to lead.</h2><div class="chapter-copy"><p>My first lessons in communication came on a basketball court. At Walddörfer SV, I coached children and teenagers, built individual development plans, and worked with players one-on-one.</p><p>A six-year-old and a sixteen-year-old don’t need the same explanation. Coaching made that impossible to ignore.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/about/">More about me</a></div></section>
  <section class="story-chapter competition-chapter" data-journey-label="Sales competition"><p class="chapter-place">Delaware · 2026</p><h2>Then, put it<br />under pressure.</h2><div class="competition-proof"><strong>Top 20</strong><span>Semi-finalist<br />Lerner Sales Competition · 122 participants</span></div><div class="chapter-copy"><p>I took on a simulated sales role presenting an oncology-focused solution. No medical background. A complex offer. A conversation that had to make sense to the client.</p><p>I learned the subject, prepared the pitch, and advanced to the semi-finals. It pushed me to turn technical information into business value—and think clearly under pressure.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/work/#sales-competition">The competition</a></div></section>
  <section class="story-chapter" data-journey-label="Client conversations"><p class="chapter-place">Hamburg · Summer 2026</p><h2>Take it into<br />client conversations.</h2><div class="chapter-copy"><p>At Horbach, I supported lead qualification and appointment setting, and shadowed senior advisors in needs-based financial planning conversations.</p><p>The lesson I’m taking into B2B sales: understand the client’s priorities before deciding what to recommend.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/experience/">My experience</a></div></section>
  <section id="work" class="story-chapter founder-story" data-journey-label="Building STRK"><div class="founder-heading"><p class="chapter-place">Now · Co-founder at STRK</p><h2>A class project<br />became a commitment.</h2></div><div class="founder-grid"><div class="founder-copy"><p>STRK started with classroom interviews and business model canvases. I kept working on the questions beyond the assignment.</p><p>{profile.interviews} My contribution included interview synthesis, business model work, and positioning as the idea evolved.</p><p>Today, we’re developing and testing a fitness coaching app with personalized plans, everyday AI guidance, and optional human trainer support. The early research shaped our direction; the current experience is what we’re testing next.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/work/strk/">Inside STRK ↗</a></div><a class="strk-art" href="/work/strk/" aria-label="Read the STRK case study"><div class="logo-panel"><img src="/assets/images/strk-wordmark-light.svg" width="720" height="300" alt="STRK light-mode wordmark" loading="lazy" /></div><span>In development. Built around real questions.</span></a></div></section>
 </div>
</div>
<section class="personal-note shell"><p class="section-label">Off the clock</p><h2>There’s more<br />than the résumé.</h2><div class="personal-note-copy"><p>Basketball. Travel. A conversation in German, English, or French. I like getting beyond the familiar—and finding something I hadn’t considered.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/about/">Meet the person behind the work</a></div><div class="personal-route" aria-label="Hamburg is home; Delaware is where I am now"><div><span>Home</span><strong>Hamburg</strong></div><span class="personal-route-track" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><span>Now</span><strong>Delaware</strong></div></div></section>
<section id="contact" class="contact-section shell"><p class="section-label">U.S. B2B sales · SDR · BDR internships</p><h2>I want to get good.<br />Let’s get to work.</h2><p class="contact-intro">If your team values preparation, direct feedback, and someone who takes the work seriously, let’s talk.</p><div class="contact-choices" id="contact-choices"><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}><span>Email me</span><strong>{profile.email}</strong><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href={profile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Connect on LinkedIn</span><strong>Start with a conversation</strong><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></div><button class="copy-address" type="button" id="copy-email" data-email={profile.email}>Copy email address</button><span id="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span></section>
<script>
const copy = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#copy-email');
copy?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
 const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#copy-status');
 try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(copy.dataset.email ?? ''); if (status) status.textContent = 'Email address copied'; }
 catch { if (status) status.textContent = 'Please select the address above to copy it'; }
});
const journey = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.story-journey');
const chapters = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.story-chapter')];
const current = journey?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.journey-current');
if (journey && chapters.length && current) {
 let queued = false;
 const updateJourney = () => {
  queued = false;
  const first = chapters[0].getBoundingClientRect();
  const last = chapters.at(-1)!.getBoundingClientRect();
  const start = window.scrollY + first.top - window.innerHeight * .45;
  const end = window.scrollY + last.bottom - window.innerHeight * .45;
  const progress = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (window.scrollY - start) / (end - start)));
  journey.style.setProperty('--journey-progress', String(progress));
  const active = [...chapters].reverse().find(chapter => chapter.getBoundingClientRect().top <= window.innerHeight * .45) ?? chapters[0];
  current.textContent = active.dataset.journeyLabel ?? '';
 };
 const scheduleJourney = () => { if (!queued) { queued = true; requestAnimationFrame(updateJourney); } };
 window.addEventListener('scroll', scheduleJourney, { passive: true });
 window.addEventListener('resize', scheduleJourney);
 updateJourney();
}
</script>
</Base>
